From 4e9c9ddf7dfb51e4eccc8ca818b54ff620f24cdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:53:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tests in float: kernels, batch integration, fixed point,
 prediction, geometry

Without SuiteSparse (MFEM in float), the sequential tests use GMRES
preconditioned by the Jacobi smoother in place of UMFPACK
(tests/SequentialLinearSolver.hxx); the checks requiring a direct solver
are skipped in this case. The CountingLinearSolver of FixedPointSolverTest
keeps the preconditioner of the wrapped solver alive.

The tolerances for float are measured (about ten times the observed
errors) and explained in comments; the tolerances for double are
unchanged.
